The dataset used in this project is a Printed Circuit Board (PCB) defect dataset derived from the DeepPCB benchmark dataset. 
It contains pairs of defect-free reference PCB images and defective PCB test images, along with annotations of six common PCB defect types.
The dataset is designed for:
Defect detection (finding differences between template and test images).
Defect localization (extracting bounding boxes around defect regions).
Defect classification (training CNN models to identify defect type).

Defect Categories
The dataset covers 6 common types of PCB defects:
Missing Hole – Drilled hole missing from the board.
Mouse Bite – Small notches on the edges of the PCB.
Open Circuit – Breaks in the copper connection.
Short Circuit – Extra copper bridging between connections.
Spur – Unwanted thin copper trace sticking out.
Spurious Copper – Extra copper areas not part of the design.

rotation/ contains rotated versions of defect images to improve model generalization.
Each defect folder has a *_angles.txt file (e.g., Spur_angles.txt) which specifies the rotation angle applied to each sample.

Annotations
XML files containing the info about the defect, bounding box coordinates and defect class labels.
